    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W3299" name="W3299. Markdown Optimization &amp; Price-Engineering Analytics" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Clearance cycle; aged inventory (W3294); margin optimization review
Frequency: Periodic + clearance events
Volume: Markdown candidate SKUs
Owner: Merchandise Planner
Participants: Merchandise Planner, Pricing (links to VS-01.2/VS-57), Category Managers, Finance (links to VS-17.1)
Source: workflow W3299 — Markdown Optimization &amp; Price-Engineering Analytics</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3299_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3299_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3299_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3299_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3299_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3299_Lane2" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3299_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3299_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3299_Start4" name="Clearance cycle; aged inventory (W3294); margin optimization review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3299_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3299_Task5" name="Merchandise Planner/Pricing run markdown optimization: model demand elasticity…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Merchandise Planner/Pricing run markdown optimization: model demand elasticity and clearance-rate by markdown depth, compute the margin-maximizing markdown cadence and timing to clear within target weeks
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Pricing
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3299_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3299_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3299_Task6" name="Category Managers select markdown depth/round per item within markdown budget…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Managers select markdown depth/round per item within markdown budget (W3285), avoid margin-destructive over-discount, and coordinate channel execution (stores, ecommerce, marketplace links to VS-65/VS-95)
Responsible (R): Category Managers / Pricing
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3299_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3299_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3299_Task7" name="Merchandise Planner/Finance measure realized markdown margin vs optimized plan…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Merchandise Planner/Finance measure realized markdown margin vs optimized plan (W3286), update elasticity model with actuals, and feed learnings to next cycle (links to VS-64.3 post-season analysis)
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3299_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3299_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3299_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3299_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3299_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-534 (ensure controlled execution — Merchandise Performance Analytics &amp; Margin Optimization (PA-101.3).) | - operational: elasticity-based optimization; operational: cadence optimization
Owner: Merchandise Planner</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
