    <bpmn:process id="W_W3300" name="W3300. Promotion Post-Mortem, Halo &amp; Cannibalization Margin Analysis" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Promotion end (links to VS-14.1/VS-58)
Frequency: Per promotion (≈6 major + monthly hot deals)
Volume: Per promo event
Owner: Merchandise Planner
Participants: Merchandise Planner, Category Managers, Marketing (links to VS-14.1), Pricing (links to VS-57), Loyalty (links to VS-13.2)
Source: workflow W3300 — Promotion Post-Mortem, Halo &amp; Cannibalization Margin Analysis</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3300_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3300_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3300_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3300_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3300_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3300_Lane2" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3300_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3300_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3300_Start4" name="Promotion end (links to VS-14.1/VS-58)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3300_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3300_Task5" name="Merchandise Planner measure promotion performance vs plan: incremental sales…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Merchandise Planner measure promotion performance vs plan: incremental sales, halo (lift on non-promoted adjacent items), cannibalization (shift from substituted items), margin vs non-promo baseline, and loyalty-member response (links to VS-13.2)
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Marketing
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per promo</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3300_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3300_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
